Content-Type: text/html; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

Effective immediately and until further notice, no Commission records may b=
e destroyed, deleted, purged or otherwise disposed of, in any medium, witho=
ut the written authorization of this office. This applies to examination wo=
rk papers, correspondence, investigative files, closed matters and prelimin=
ary inquiries alike, and it applies regardless of what any existing disposi=
tion schedule says.<br />
<br />
Two consequences for day-to-day work.<br />
<br />
Electronic mail is included. The journal capture on the messaging system re=
mains on and its retention period is suspended, so nothing ages out. Do not=
 treat a message as gone because it is no longer in your mailbox; the journ=
al copy exists independently of what you keep or delete.<br />
<br />
Local copies are not a substitute. If you are holding examination correspon=
dence on a share drive or in personal folders, that is fine, but the author=
itative copy for retention purposes is the journal copy. Do not delete anyt=
hing on the theory that the system of record already has it.<br />
